<section id="how-it-works" tabindex="-1" class="story-process" aria-labelledby="process-title"><div class="container story-section">
<div class="story-heading" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">02 / FROM DATA TO DECISIONS</span><h2 id="process-title">A useful answer starts<br>with what you know.</h2><p>Begin with bills, interval readings, or both. Each gives your team a different kind of context.</p></div>
<div class="story-data-paths grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2" data-reveal><article><span class="eyebrow">MONTHLY BILLS</span><h3>Understand spending over time.</h3><p>Enter a bill’s period, kWh, and amount. With at least two months, compare changes in usage and spending. Bill-only buildings do not produce a demand forecast.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">INTERVAL READINGS</span><h3>See when demand happens.</h3><p>Upload a <code>timestamp,kwh</code> CSV. Caldren checks timestamps, kWh values, and duplicate timestamps within the file.</p><code class="story-csv">2026-10-01 09:00,42.6</code></article></div>
<div class="story-scene story-scene-reverse" data-scroll-scene><figure class="story-stage"><img src="{{ asset('images/caldren-building-dusk.webp') }}" alt="Commercial office building illuminated at dusk" loading="lazy" width="1536" height="1024" data-scene-image><figcaption><span>THE BUILDING STORY</span><strong data-scene-caption>01 / Set up</strong></figcaption></figure><div class="story-chapters"><article data-story-step data-caption="01 / Set up"><span class="eyebrow">01 / SET UP</span><h3>Create a home for your buildings.</h3><p>Create an organization and add each site’s location, time zone, and standard energy rate. Add peak rates and hours when relevant. Workspace owners can invite teammates.</p><span class="story-footnote">Start with one building. Add the wider portfolio when you are ready.</span></article>
<article data-story-step data-caption="02 / Import"><span class="eyebrow">02 / IMPORT</span><h3>Bring in the history.</h3><p>Upload interval readings or record monthly bills for the right building. The import checks formatting and values before saving. Recent coverage is checked separately when you request an outlook.</p><span class="story-footnote">Only bills? Record at least two months to start seeing spending and usage trends.</span></article>
<article data-story-step data-caption="03 / Estimate"><span class="eyebrow">03 / ESTIMATE</span><h3>Look seven days ahead.</h3><p>Forecasts require at least 14 complete days of recent hourly or sub-hourly readings with sufficient daily coverage. Caldren sends bounded daily summaries, a historical baseline, time zone, and tariff settings to the OpenAI API. Returned estimates are checked against the history.</p><span class="story-footnote">Missing coverage? Add recent readings. Generation unavailable? Your history stays visible and you can retry.</span></article>
<article data-story-step data-caption="04 / Decide together"><span class="eyebrow">04 / DECIDE TOGETHER</span><h3>Put building knowledge first.</h3><p>Review possible peak alerts and tariff-aware suggestions with your facility team. Compare the outlook with actual conditions before changing schedules or equipment settings.</p><span class="story-footnote">Caldren supports human review. It does not control equipment or guarantee savings.</span></article>
</div></div></div></section>
